1	e11e7470-a3ff-4096-9078-c75d969856a2	2025-03-11 16:16:48.642327+00	Software Engineer Intern\n	As a Software Engineer Intern, you will gain hands-on experience in analyzing, designing, coding, and testing various components of application code across one or more clients. Your day-to-day tasks will involve assisting with maintenance, enhancements, and development work while collaborating with experienced engineers to build and improve software solutions.\n	["Developing small to medium size automation/applications (coding, programming)", "Debugging and testing code", "Help senior developers with the documentations and software testing", "Collaborate and participate with technical discussions with senior developers and leaders", "Proactively learning about new technologies"]	["Enrolled in an internship subject", "Able to pass the pre-internship requirements", "Basic experience working on a web development project using Javascript, CSS, HTML , Bootstrap , Node.js , Jquery", "Software Development Life Cycle", "Database Management: Basic understanding of database systems and proficiency in SQL or NoSQL databases.", "Basic Fundamentals with any programming languages (Java, C#, C++)", "Basic Fundamentals in Web Development (Javascript, HTML, CSS, Bootstrap, Node.js , Jquery)", "Can understand basic documentations (Technical Documentations , Test Plans)", "Willing to work onsite or hybrid"]	8 hour shift	Monday - Friday	5	t	3
7	e6cef650-f15d-4319-81c6-dc9f31d28817	2025-03-20 09:27:14.126996+00	Cloud DevOps Intern	As a Cloud DevOps Intern, you will play a key role in automating cloud infrastructure, streamlining software deployment, and enhancing system reliability. You will work alongside experienced DevOps engineers, gaining hands-on experience in CI/CD pipelines, cloud automation, infrastructure as code (IaC), and monitoring tools. This internship provides an excellent opportunity to develop technical expertise in cloud-native technologies and learn industry best practices for ensuring system scalability, security, and performance.	["Assist in configuring, optimizing, and troubleshooting CI/CD pipelines to automate software deployment across cloud environments.", "Work with Jenkins, GitHub Actions, and GitLab CI/CD to streamline development workflows.", "Gain hands-on experience with Docker and Kubernetes for containerization and orchestration.", "Help containerize applications, manage deployments, and implement scaling strategies for cloud-native systems.", "Learn and apply Infrastructure-as-Code (IaC) principles using Terraform and Ansible to provision and manage cloud resources.", "Assist in automating cloud application deployment using cloud automation tools and setting up monitoring solutions.", "Explore Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) methodologies to optimize system performance and improve fault tolerance.", "Work on cloud security best practices, implementing access controls, encryption, and compliance policies.", "Collaborate with developers, cloud engineers, and security teams to ensure smooth DevOps integration.", "Assist in documenting DevOps workflows and best practices."]	["Currently pursuing or recently completed a degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Engineering, or a related field.", "Understanding of CI/CD tools such as Jenkins, GitHub Actions, GitLab CI/CD, or CircleCI.", "Basic knowledge of containerization technologies like Docker and container orchestration with Kubernetes.", "Experience with cloud automation tools such as Terraform, Ansible, or Bash scripting.", "Proficiency in scripting languages like Python, Go, or Shell scripting is a plus.", "Familiarity with monitoring/logging tools like Prometheus, Grafana, ELK Stack, or CloudWatch is a bonus.", "Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with a keen interest in cloud automation and DevOps practices.", "Ability to work in a fast-paced environment, learn quickly, and collaborate effectively with a team."]	8 hour shift	Monday - Friday	5	t	5
18	e6d97520-630f-4854-869e-a622b738f283	2025-04-09 13:51:23.012085+00	Data Analytics Intern	We are looking for a Data Analytics Intern to support our team in analyzing financial data to drive strategic decisions. This role involves working with large datasets, creating reports, and providing insights that will influence business operations and customer engagement strategies.	["Collect and analyze data from various sources", "Develop dashboards and reports to visualize data insights", "Assist in identifying trends and patterns in financial data", "Collaborate with different departments to understand data needs", "Ensure data accuracy and integrity in all analyses"]	["Currently pursuing a degree in Statistics, Data Science, Economics, or related field", "Proficient in data analysis tools such as Excel, SQL, or Python", "Experience with data visualization tools like Tableau or Power BI", "Strong analytical and critical thinking skills", "Excellent communication skills to present findings clearly"]	\N	\N	2	t	2
